### 3. Student Loan Interest Deduction
You paid $4,800 in student loan interest, but the IRS caps this deduction at **$2,500** per year. 
Furthermore, this deduction is subject to a Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) phase-out. For 2023, the phase-out for single filers begins at $75,000 and is completely eliminated at **$90,000**. 
